anger to myself  because this whole situation enrages me  so much  then i'm likely to get myself into  trouble um  you know we all know you have to get a  test  before flying i could live with that if  they took the results seriously  um okay fine i booked my lateral flow  test  with some difficulty because these  things are never simple  you know anything online is horribly  complicated  but i i i managed uh with a  great deal of self congratulations and i  went to the wrong testing center first  and then we  practically ran to the one on the fifth  floor terminal two  to make sure we got to our 410  appointment  um the experience was one of  relative efficiency given the  inefficiency of the entire business  but you know if you believe that the  tests are accurate  and therefore you have an entire load of  passengers who  are not infected with covid19  why do we have to wear masks you know  and that's even assuming that they work  which of course  they don't so that pantomime is  exasperating  and that's one of the reasons that air  rage  incidents especially in the united  states are going through the roof  and uh in my column i called attention  to  an incident that went viral last month  in which a poor flight attendant was  uh not only bloodied but lost two teeth  now the debate in uk government is  ultimately pushing towards harder border  restrictions  than any easing no no country's added to  the green list on the latest update  few expect there to be next time and i  think there seems to be this argument  developing  that actually tighter borders  particularly to countries like new  zealand and australia means greater  domestic freedoms it's what several  cabinet ministers are pushing  um do you think perhaps they do have a  point and  maybe traveling is just something that  is nice  uh that's what some would say but  ultimately domestic freedoms are gonna  count first  okay that's a very peculiar definition  of domestic freedom  not you know freedom not t