reness of aging and  mortality  um and maybe in in the wrong direction  it's made people  more fearful uh more risk averse  and i i wish it were working the other  direction  um if there's any lesson in  my new novel which i hope is mostly just  exercise and share entertainment um  then it's that we need to be more  intentioned  in relation to the end of our life  and to apply the same kind of intention  to  our old age and inevitable death  as we do to the other parts of our our  lives i mean we plan  we plan to be uh  whatever when we grow up uh we  make decisions about marriage and family  you know we have a sense of direction  it's often subverted  but we don't want to we just don't want  to think about  the the last bit and  the the pandemic has forced us to  to think a little more about the the  last bit because it's been up in our  face in  broadcast newscasting and i  to agree if if we if we apply that  greater awareness in a positive way  that's that's not a bad thing  if we instead just become more and more  terrified uh well that's just  that's just a formula for not just  living and then dying but not  living at all  [Music]  you

